intent_record.intent_summary:
{
  "what": "The helper function `dsa_dev_to_net_device()` was removed entirely. In `dsa_port_parse()`, the `"cpu"` branch no longer calls that helper; instead it acquires `rtnl_lock()`, searches for a class `"net"` child device with `dev_find_class()`, returns `-EPROBE_DEFER` if none is found, converts the device to a `net_device`, takes a tracked reference with `netdev_hold(&dp->conduit_tracker, GFP_KERNEL)`, releases the device with `put_device()`, unlocks RTNL, then calls `dsa_port_parse_cpu()`. If that call fails, it drops the netdevice reference with `netdev_put()` before returning the error.",
  "how": "This changes conduit acquisition from an untracked `dev_hold()`/`dev_put()`-based lookup to a tracked `net_device` lifetime management scheme tied to `dp->conduit_tracker`, while also serializing the lookup with the rtnl lock. At runtime, it prevents the conduit netdevice from disappearing during CPU-port parsing, and ensures the reference is properly released if parsing fails. It also preserves deferred probing when the net class device is not yet available.",
  "change_category": "bug_fix",
  "intent_summary": "Fix CPU port parsing to safely acquire and track the conduit net_device under RTNL and release it on failure."
}

